================================================================================

   Except with Written Permission or under a Commercial License, You may not,
   and You may not allow, assist or encourage anyone else to:

   4.1  Commercial Use.
        Engage in Commercial Use of the Software, a Fork or a Derivative Work.

   4.2  Production Use.
        Engage in Production Use of the Software, a Fork or a Derivative Work,
        for any purpose and for any person, including You, Your employer, Your
        friends, Your community or Your own side project.

   4.3  Hosting and service offerings.
        Provide the Software, a Fork or a Derivative Work, or any substantial
        part of its functionality, to third parties as a hosted service, a
        managed service, a platform, an API, a control plane, a template, a
        starter kit, a one-click deployment, a marketplace listing, a plugin
        for a commercial platform, or in any similar way, with or without
        charge.

   4.4  Private Copies and closed derivatives.
        Keep a Private Copy, a private mirror or a closed-source Derivative
        Work for any use other than the short-term, local, personal reading
        and Development Use that Section 2 allows. Distribution of any
        Derivative Work, in source or in object form, is permitted only as a
        Public Fork.

   4.5  Sublicensing, relicensing, selling.
        Sublicense, relicense, sell, rent, lease, lend, pledge, or transfer
        the Software or any right under this License, except as Section 11
        describes, or remove or replace this License with another one.

   4.6  Competing offerings.
        Use the Software, its documentation, its schemas, its protocols, its
        decision records, or its design to build, operate, market, train or
        benchmark a product or service that competes with ExponetDB or with
        another product of the Licensor, even if You wrote all the code
        yourself, where the use depends on knowledge, expression or material
        You took from the Software beyond ordinary facts, ideas and
        techniques that are not protected by law.

   4.7  Circumvention.
        Remove, disable, obscure or evade a notice, a header, a provenance
        statement, a license check, a usage limit or any technical or
        contractual measure that the Software or the Licensor uses to enforce
        this License.

   4.8  Misrepresentation.
        State or imply that the Licensor made, wrote, certified, audited,
        approved, sponsors or endorses You, Your Fork, Your service or Your
        product, or that the Software is open source.

   4.9  Unlawful use.
        Use the Software to violate any law, to infringe the rights of others,
        to attack systems or people, or to process personal data without a
        legal basis.

   4.10 Sanctions and restricted use.
        Use or export the Software in violation of applicable sanctions or
        export-control laws, or make it available to a person or in a place
        that those laws prohibit.

   4.11 Misuse of the Licensor's name or likeness.
        Use the name, the handle, the picture or the likeness of the Licensor
        in a way that suggests a relationship with You, other than the
        attribution this License requires.

   An action that this Section prohibits is a breach of this License and, where
   it also exceeds the scope of the permissions in Section 2, an infringement
   of the Licensor's copyright, because no license covers it.


