 9. SECURITY RESEARCH AND VULNERABILITY REPORTS
================================================================================

   9.1  Good-faith research.
        The Licensor welcomes good-faith security research on the Software.
        Reading, analyzing and running the Software in a local lab against
        synthetic data to find vulnerabilities is permitted under this License,
        even though it is not a Public Fork, as long as You (a) do not attack
        systems that You do not own or have permission to test, in particular
        any deployment of ExponetDB run by the Licensor or by anyone else;
        (b) do not access, change or keep data of other people; (c) do not
        disrupt any service; and (d) report what You find as described in
        SECURITY.md before You publish it, and give the Licensor a reasonable
        time to fix it.

   9.2  Reporting channel.
        Vulnerabilities are reported privately, as SECURITY.md describes. Do
        not open a public issue with exploit details for an unfixed problem.

   9.3  Safe harbor.
        The Licensor will not bring a claim under this License against research
        that follows this Section. This is not a promise about the conduct of
        any third party or about what the law of Your country requires of You.


