 12. TERMINATION, CURE AND REINSTATEMENT
================================================================================

   12.1 Automatic termination.
        If You breach this License, Your rights under it end automatically,
        without notice, on the date of the breach, except as 12.3 provides.

   12.2 Consequences.
        When Your rights end, You immediately stop all use of the Software, stop
        all Production Use and Commercial Use, take down any Public Fork that
        You could not lawfully keep, delete Private Copies, and stop
        distributing. Sections that by their nature should survive survive,
        including 1, 3.8, 4, 5.7, 6, 8, 11.3, 13 to 18.

   12.3 Cure for a first, unintended breach.
        If this is Your first breach, and it was not deliberate, Your rights
        are reinstated provisionally if You (a) stop the breaching conduct
        within thirty (30) days after You learn of the breach or the Licensor
        tells You in writing, whichever is earlier, and (b) tell the Licensor
        what happened. Reinstatement becomes permanent if the Licensor does not
        object in writing within sixty (60) days after Your notice. A second
        breach, or a deliberate one, is not eligible for cure.

   12.4 Reinstatement by the Licensor.
        The Licensor may at any time reinstate Your rights in writing, on
        conditions of the Licensor's choice.

   12.5 Termination for patent or license claims.
        See Section 2.7. Rights also end if You challenge the validity or
        enforceability of this License, or of the Licensor's rights in the
        Software, to the extent the law allows that consequence.

   12.6 Other remedies.
        Termination does not limit any other remedy that the Licensor has,
        including injunctive relief, damages, an account of profits, a
        reasonable license fee for past use, and recovery of reasonable legal
        costs, as far as the law allows.

   12.7 Licensor's right to stop distribution.
        The Licensor may stop publishing the Software, or a Release of it, at
        any time. Rights in copies that You lawfully received before that
        remain, within this License.


